  "result": "I fixed the duplication in `src/lib/event-bus.ts`. The existing event-bus tests pass (9/9). I did not add a regression test or run the detach/re-attach cycle end to end.\n\nThe cause was in `subscribe()`. Each subscribe copies the handler set and replaces it. The returned unsubscribe, though, deleted from the set captured at subscribe time. Once a later handler was added for the same event type, detaching an earlier handler removed it from a stale copy, so it stayed attached. Each detach/re-attach cycle left another live copy behind. That explains the duplicated webhooks, audit rows and usage increments. Notifications were never duplicated because their handlers are attached once at module load and never detached.\n\nThe unsubscribe now removes the handler from the set that is live at detach time. It is also idempotent, so calling it twice is harmless.",
